      "writtenOn": "2024-10-09T23:54:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "@danakj, can you PTAL?\n\nThe high-level problem is that we need a `cxx.h` include path that can be used **both** in Chromium and in Skia.  I think the path used in Chromium (`third_party/rust/cxx/v1/cxx.h`) won\u0027t necessarily work for Skia and Skia\u0027s customers.  And I think that we may also want to change the path used in Chromium to provide a different version-agnostic mechanism (currently we have a forwarding header at [`third_party/rust/cxx/v1/cxx.h`](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/rust/cxx/v1/cxx.h;drc\u003d93b1a3d042cdca0b19fa993266e12f4aec924414)).\n\nThe short include path is provided by Skia-authored [`BUILD.bazel.skia`](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/skia/bazel/external/cxx/BUILD.bazel.skia;l\u003d27-38;drc\u003d1c4f4684ff50b3f8ef8ea0735b04cfef58ff46bd). \n Maybe we can use Bazel\u0027s [`include_prefix`](https://bazel.build/reference/be/c-cpp#cc_library.include_prefix) option to inject something here?\n \nWDYT?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 14,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 14,
        "endChar": 24
      },
      "revId": "4647bc3d2ca812c91255943aa71b1e49e801b47e",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "03b99b26_fa19220f",
        "filename": "experimental/rust_png/impl/SkPngRustCodec.h",
